## Conventions that are not obvious from the code

<!--
  The highest-value section. Things a competent engineer would get wrong on
  their first week here.

  Examples of the right shape:
  - Errors: raise domain exceptions from core/, translate to HTTP only in api/
  - New endpoints go in api/v2/. api/v1/ is frozen.
  - All timestamps are UTC and stored as timezone-aware datetimes.
  - Use the repository pattern in adapters/; no ORM queries in core/.
  - Tests use factories from tests/factories.py, never fixtures.
-->

